detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — maximize total profit (unit price minus raw material cost minus operating costs), minimize total operating cost, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The \"Operating Costs at Full Capacity\" column — is this a fixed cost incurred whenever the machine is used at all (regardless of how much), or is it a cost that scales proportionally with the fraction of capacity actually used?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the cost structure (fixed vs. proportional), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any demand limits or minimum production requirements for each product, or can the factory produce and sell any quantity of each product as long as machine capacity allows?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the existence of demand limits or minimum production requirements versus unlimited production within capacity."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the fixed operating cost of a machine — is it incurred only if that machine is used for at least one product, or is it incurred for the machine as a whole as long as it is used for any product (i.e., one shared fixed cost per machine regardless of which products run on it)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question about the nature of the fixed operating cost (per-product usage vs. shared per-machine cost), which is one semantically independent decision point."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "is the quantity of each product that enters procedure A required to equal the quantity that enters procedure B (i.e., one unit of finished product needs exactly one unit of A-time and one unit of B-time)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the relationship between quantities in procedures A and B."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can the production quantity of each product be fractional (e.g., 10.5 units), or must it be a whole number of units?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the granularity of production quantities (fractional vs. integer)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "If a machine is not used at all, its fixed operating cost is zero — is that correct, meaning the fixed cost is only charged when the machine's total assigned processing time is greater than zero?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question about the condition under which fixed operating costs are incurred."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the profit calculation, is the selling price (unit price) the only revenue, and is the raw material cost the only per-unit variable cost — so that profit per unit of product I is 1.25 − 0.25 = 1.00, product II is 2.00 − 0.35 = 1.65, and product III is 2.80 − 0.50 = 2.30, before subtracting the fixed machine operating costs?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single confirmation of the profit calculation assumptions (revenue and variable cost definitions) to validate the derived per-unit profits."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the effective machine hours (e.g., A1 = 6000, A2 = 10000) the total available hours for the entire planning period?",
    "Is the processing time in the table (e.g., 5 for product I on A1) the hours required per unit of product?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two distinct clarification requests: one regarding the scope of the machine hours (total available vs. other) and another regarding the definition of the processing time values (per unit vs. other). These can be answered independently."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "If a machine is used for some products but not others, the fixed cost is still just the single listed amount for that machine — so for example, if A1 is used only for product I (not product II), the cost is still 300 yuan, not 300 plus anything extra?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation on how fixed costs are applied when a machine is used for only a subset of products."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any limit on how many units of a single product can be processed on a given machine, or can all of a product's A-time be assigned to one machine (e.g., all of product I's procedure A on A1 alone)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding capacity limits or assignment constraints for a product on a machine."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can a single product's procedure A be split across both A1 and A2 (e.g., some units of product I on A1 and the rest on A2), or must each product's procedure A be assigned to exactly one machine?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding whether a product's procedure can be split across machines or must be assigned to one, which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can a single product's procedure B also be split across multiple B machines (e.g., some units of product I on B1 and the rest on B2), or must each product's procedure B be assigned to exactly one machine?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding whether splitting is allowed or if exclusive assignment is required."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any relationship or constraint between which A machine processes a unit and which B machine processes it — for example, must a unit processed on A1 for procedure A also be processed on a specific B machine for procedure B, or are the A and B assignments completely independent?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking about the dependency or independence between A and B machine assignments."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any other costs or constraints I should account for besides the raw material cost per unit, the fixed machine operating costs, and the machine hour capacity limits?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking if there are additional costs or constraints beyond the ones already listed."
}
